vuelta config init — detect a project and create validated configuration

Examples:
  vuelta config init .
  vuelta config init . --no-input --stack node --package-manager npm --branch main --remote origin

Usage:
  vuelta config init [options] <project-path> [config-path]

Options:
  --stack STACK              select python, node, or docker
  --package-manager NAME     select the Python or Node package manager
  --compose-file PATH        set the project-relative Compose file
  --test-service NAME        set the Compose test service
  --branch NAME              set the protected branch
  --remote NAME              set the Git remote
  --allow-path PATH          allow a changed path (repeatable)
  --docker-file PATH         select a Dockerfile (repeatable)
  --runtime-image DIGEST     set an immutable runtime image (repeatable)
  --force                    overwrite an existing config
  --non-interactive          legacy alias for --no-input

Defaults:
  Config: operating system user config path unless --config or config-path is set.
  Boolean options: disabled unless specified.

Global options:
  -c, --config PATH          use an alternate config.yaml
  --no-input                 disable prompts; does not confirm changes
  --no-color                 disable color and terminal formatting
  -h, --help                 show help and exit
  --version                  show version and exit

Security:
  --force replaces an existing configuration; review the destination path first.
